WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

STYLE
::cue { color: white }

NOTE written by hand for the tests

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.600
So, has everyone heard of a lighthouse?

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.100
I would be surprised if you hadn't.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.600
It is a tower --
it guides ships --

cue-4
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.100
and it has stood on coasts for centuries

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.600
which makes it a good story to start with.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.100
Why does the light turn?

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.600
Why is it so tall?

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.100
And my favourite question:

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.600
who looked after it?

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.100
Keepers lived there all year &amp; kept the lamp lit.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.600
They trimmed the wick every night.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.100
They wound the clockwork that turned the lens.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.600
The lens bent the light into a beam.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:04.100
Ships far away could see it flash.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.600
Each lighthouse had its own pattern.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.100
Sailors learnt the patterns by heart.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.600
That told them where they were.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.100
Today most lights run on their own.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.600
But the towers still stand.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.100
And people still visit them.
